{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"bea9b0d13eed511177d58e672977aa9cca110d18217abcb924f05528af6e9115","digest":{"component_or_area":"plan-review gate / operator-attested completion evidence","key_entities":["ADR 0043","docs/adr/0043-operator-attested-completion-evidence.md","src/rebar/_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/material_diff.py","src/rebar/llm/completion.py","COMPLETION_REMEDIATION_GUIDANCE","[operator-attested]","stale-material","material fingerprint"],"problem_keywords":["operator-attested evidence","plan review gate","material invalidation","agent authorship","completion evidence","documentation clarification"],"propositions":["Documentation must clarify that operator-attested describes evidence location, not actor identity, and that agents may provide truthful concrete evidence they observed.","The [operator-attested] marker must be added to criterion text before plan review to avoid material invalidation on description edits.","Concrete evidence should be recorded in ticket comments, which are non-material and do not invalidate signed plan attestations.","The existing exact-tag, specificity, and command-versus-attestation safeguards must remain in ADR 0043 and the plan-writing guide.","Adding the marker after plan certification edits plan material and causes stale-material rejection; the marker must be present before certification or evidence must use a separate non-material representation."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1786342885749544041,"uuid":"f3817654-b23a-4d36-8ce3-716c3865ec82"}